course: dictionary
lesson: 11537
title: Changed or altered?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Alter means to change something, to make it different. When you meet «altered», look at the words around it to find out what changed and why. «The dress was too big, so Mum altered it to fit me.» Too big is the clue: the dress was changed so it would fit.
explain: Altered can also describe a thing that has already been changed. «The photo had been altered on a computer, so it was not really true.» Here altered is an adjective, a word that describes the photo. Ask yourself: what word would fit in this spot? Then swap in changed and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Scientists use altered in a special way. «In our science test, we altered only the water, so it was a fair test.» Only one thing is changed on purpose, and everything else stays the same. That is what makes the test fair.
fact: Altered means changed or made different.
fact: As an adjective, altered describes something that has been changed, such as an altered photo.
fact: «Altered» can also describe a pet that has had an operation so it cannot have babies. This is a polite, grown-up way of saying it.
fact: A good check is to swap changed into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Clothes are often altered to fit better, and photos can be altered on a computer, so not every picture is true.
exercise: «The dress was too big, so Mum altered it to fit me.» What does altered mean here? | Washed in hot water | *Changed to make it a different size | Thrown in the bin | Put away in a cupboard
exercise: «The photo had been altered on a computer, so it was not really true.» What kind of word is altered here, and what does it describe? | A verb, meaning to look at a photo | A noun, meaning a camera | *An adjective, describing a photo that has been changed | A verb, meaning to take a photo
exercise: Which word means the same as altered? | fixed | *changed | hidden | stayed
test: «In our science test, we altered only the water, so it was a fair test.» What does altered mean? | Hidden | *Changed | Forgotten | Measured
test: Which word describes a photo that has been changed? | cloudy | blurry | *altered | pretty
exam: «The recipe was altered by Dad, so it had less sugar.» What did Dad do to the recipe? | *Changed it | Lost it | Copied it exactly | Read it aloud
